2026-10-29T14:44:49.8278674Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8383481Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8393985Z [0m
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8395537Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8396151Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8396499Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8396964Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8397680Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8397973Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8398231Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8398633Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8398805Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8399645Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8400373Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8400841Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8401199Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8401580Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8401821Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8402086Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8402359Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8402736Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8402866Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8402984Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8403134Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8403506Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8404008Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8408318Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8408514Z I will:
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8408710Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8409059Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8409628Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8410122Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8410538Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8410902Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8411198Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8411677Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8412046Z    /root
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8424068Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8425356Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8436844Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8437453Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8437944Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8439292Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8440018Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8465696Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8466309Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8477581Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8478431Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8478931Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8479131Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8479315Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8479554Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8479817Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8480265Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8480470Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8480589Z If you would like to
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8480876Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8481051Z 
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8481274Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-29T14:44:49.8481627Z   $ sh ./install-nix
